'''Gotals''' were a [[species]] of [[humanoid]] [[Sentience|sentients]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[moon]] [[Antar 4]]. They were common throughout the galaxy and could be seen on many planets.

==Biology and appearance==
Gotals were a [[species]] of tall, [[humanoid]] [[Sentience|sentients]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[moon]] [[Antar 4]]. Their most distinctive features were the twin conical horns growing on the top of their heads, which acted as highly responsive electro-magnetic sensors and caused [[Headache|discomfort]] when exposed to complex electrical systems, like [[droid]]s. Gotals were also covered with distinctive short [[Hair|fur]]<ref name="Gotal" /> that was prone to shedding.<ref name="Tarkin" />

==History==
Gotals were part of galactic society as far back as the early days of the Galactic Republic, and were represented in the Galactic Senate as well as the [[Jedi Order]].<ref name="Tarkin" /> Around [[300 BBY]],<ref name="GotalDate">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates ''[[The Vow of Silver Dawn]]'' to [[200 BBY]].. The book says that the disappearance of the [[Gotal]] happened about a hundred years before, thus the event took place around [[300 BBY]].</ref> a group of Gotal in the [[Aakaash system]] vanished, and the [[Land & Sky Corporation]] that ruled over the [[star system]] failed to explain what had happened. Thus, many Gotal chose to avoid the Aakaash system, making the species a rare sight within its borders.<ref name="Vow">''[[The Vow of Silver Dawn]]''</ref> Throughout the [[Separatist Crisis]], their homeworld of Antar 4 was held by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], leading to a diaspora that had many Gotals flee to the colony world of [[Atzerri]].<ref name="Tarkin" />

==Gotals in the galaxy==
[[File:Gotal_Gambler_FC.png|thumb|left|250px|A Gotal con artist.]]
Gotals were often seen off-world on [[planet]]s such as [[Coruscant]], [[Tatooine]],<ref name="Sphere of Influence">{{TCW|Sphere of Influence}}</ref> [[Lothal]],<ref name="Spark" /> [[Castilon]],<ref name="The Recruit">{{Resistance|The Recruit}}</ref> and on the [[moon]] of [[Pantora]].<ref name="Cornered" /> Many Gotal were sympathetic to the Empire.<ref name="HttJ">''[[Heir to the Jedi]]''</ref>

A [[Gender|male]] Gotal named [[Barrisk Favvin]] worked for the [[Imperial Security Bureau]].<ref name="HttJ" />

Another Gotal named [[Feltipern Trevagg]] worked as a a tax collector in the [[city]] of [[Mos Eisley]], Tatooine. In the [[Standard day|days]] preceding the [[Battle of Yavin]], Trevagg was courting [[M'iiyoom Onith]], unaware of the inherent dangers of romancing a female [[H'nemthe (species)|H'nemthe]].<ref name="CL 2016">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref>

